1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
We have to assume that this is the work
of a Conjurer.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Killua] You're right. No doubt about it.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
These buildings weren't here yesterday.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,000
This has to be Nen.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Oh, man, these guys are out
of their minds.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
They have someone who can conjure up
entire buildings!

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
We should be prepared
for any traps they've set.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
[Killua] Yeah. It also pretty much proves
they're still around here somewhere.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The problem is these buildings create
way too many blind spots.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
I can only see 20 percent
of the area at one time.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
[Kurapika]
But if you move around too much,

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
there's a chance you might
run into one of them.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I'd really like to avoid that.

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The thing is, I have no idea what I'd do
if I heard their voices behind me.

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
My heart is already pounding.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
-Voices, huh?
-[Killua] What?

17
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Nothing. Never mind.

18
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Just go back to your post
for the time being.

19
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
I'll call you back in five minutes.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Melody. How are things going on your end?

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
-We're still shopping.
-[Neon] I wanna see that one!

22
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
This is harder than normal bodyguard work.

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
-[Neon] I guess it's not too bad.
-I think Basho's about to snap.

24
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
[Neon] Let's go back to the other store!

25
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Okay, I understand.

26
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
[crashing]

27
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
[theme music playing]

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Beloved x And x Beleaguered

29
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Chrollo] Just to be perfectly clear,
you've already told me

30
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
everything Uvo knew about the chain user?

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[Shalnark] Yeah.
When we were investigating

32
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
the Nostrade family
using the Hunter website,

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Uvo pointed out the three at the top
as the members he thought he recognized.

34
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
It was late on the night of the first,
when we realized

35
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
that they were the daughter's bodyguards.

36
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
And the girl... it was just yesterday
when I met her.

37
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
That's when you stole her ability,
wasn't it?

38
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
-The first time you made contact?
-[Chrollo] Yes.

39
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,000
And here is an updated list
of all the bodyguards in question.

40
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
There are two new members.

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Oh, wow.

42
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
They already updated it?
That was so fast.

43
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
So I count seven bodyguards.
There might even be more than that.

44
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
That's an awful lot of people
to guard one little girl.

45
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
[Phinks] He loves his daughter.

46
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
[Chrollo] More like he holds her ability
in higher regard than the girl herself.

47
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Her father got to where he is today
by capitalizing on her power.

48
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:52,000
And of course, there are many
who resent his advancement.

49
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
But why did she come to Yorknew City
in the first place?

50
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
My guess, she's here for the auction.

51
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
[thunder crashing]

52
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Are you okay?

53
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
[Chrollo] Shizuku, Pakunoda.

54
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
[Pakunoda] We're listening.

55
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Nice.

56
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
How could I have been so blind?
Damn it, what's wrong with me?

57
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Nostrade's daughter comes to Yorknew City.
Why? If only I had thought about it...

58
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
perhaps we could have found
the chain user sooner.

59
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
It's safe to assume that this girl
came to Yorknew for the auction,

60
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
along with her bodyguards.

61
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,000
I was too focused on her fortune-telling
ability to give it much thought.

62
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
According to the website,
she's known to collect certain body parts.

63
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
It would seem that's her hobby.

64
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Body parts? The Scarlet Eyes!

65
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
That's right.

66
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Which means that the chain user joined
the Nostrade family for a reason.

67
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
He knew that the Scarlet Eyes
would be sold at the auction

68
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
and that Nostrade's daughter
would be interested in buying them.

69
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
The chain user wants two things.

70
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
To exact revenge on us
and retrieve the eyes.

71
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Okay, Shal, what about the Scarlet Eyes?
Were we able to retrieve them?

72
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Sorry, but I'm not sure.

73
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,000
I had the auctioneer running on autopilot
for pretty much the whole auction.

74
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Chrollo] Kortopi, do you remember
copying the Scarlet Eyes?

75
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Yes, I did.

76
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
[Chrollo] Your copies function as your En.

77
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
So can you tell where the copy is?

78
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Yes, if I'm touching the original.

79
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,000
I found them.

80
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
[Kortopi] Got it.

81
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
There's something of the same shape
in that direction,

82
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
approximately 2,500 meters.

83
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
[Nobunaga] Is the chain user there?

84
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[Kortopi] We should hurry.

85
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
The effects of the En will fade
in a few hours.

86
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Do you have the map?

87
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[Phinks] Here.

88
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
[Chrollo] North by northwest...

89
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Twenty-five-hundred meters...

90
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
The Beitacle Hotel.

91
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[Nobunaga] Boss...

92
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Let me go check it out.
I beg you.

93
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Very well.

94
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
-[gasps]
-[Chrollo] But I'm coming with you.

95
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
-You got it.
-Paku, Machi, Shizuku.

96
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
You're coming, too.

97
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
-Shal, you'll switch with Kortopi.
-Okay.

98
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
[phone vibrating]

99
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,000
[Killua] Hello?

100
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
-[Melody] Is this Killua?
-[Killua] Yeah, who are you?

101
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[Melody] One of Kurapika's colleagues.
Could you look to your left?

102
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Hang up and whisper a command to me.
Anything at all.

103
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Raise your right hand.

104
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[Killua] That's a hell of an ear!
That's gonna come in handy.

105
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
[Nobunaga]
Really? Didn't we already go there before?

106
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
I thought the Beitacle Hotel...

107
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Isn't that one of the places
the Nostrade family was staying?

108
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
It was, but by the time Shal got to look
at the Hunter website,

109
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
they had already checked out
of their rooms.

110
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
[Chrollo] They probably checked
back into the same hotel

111
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
under a different name.
They're being cautious.

112
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
The rain makes it difficult
to make out what they're saying,

113
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
but there's a group of people
talking over there.

114
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:35,000
There are five or six of them,
including some women.

115
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
And they're all headed
away from those abandoned buildings.

116
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
That's amazing.

117
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Gon and I have done a lot of training
but I can’t hear that.

118
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Because it’s my ability.

119
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
For Kurapika to ask me for my help,

120
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
I’m guessing he must be getting
really desperate.

121
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Think so?

122
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
He wants to do everything by himself,
doesn't he?

123
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Oh, you're right. He sure does.

124
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Would you happen to be an assassin?

125
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Well, I used to be. How did you know?

126
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Melody] Your footsteps.

127
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
You're right beside me,
but they're estinto.

128
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Esti-what?

129
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Estinto. It's a musical term
that means they're just barely audible.

130
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
[Killua] Oh. I guess I’m in the habit
of moving silently.

131
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[Melody] Yours are the quietest
I've ever heard.

132
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Your technique is very impressive.

133
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
It's easy to see why Kurapika
would rely on you.

134
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Maybe. But I’m not too thrilled
about this.

135
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Oh, is that so?

136
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
[gasps] Wait, stop.

137
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:42,000
They're 100 meters away,
just around the next corner.

138
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
You can pick out their footsteps?

139
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Each person’s has their own unique sound.

140
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Oh. I'll check it out.

141
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
[phone ringing]

142
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Hey, Killua.

143
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
-[Killua] The woman's here.
-She is?

144
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
[Killua] She's with her buddies.
There are six of them.

145
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
-The guy with the topknot’s here, too.
-[Gon groans]

146
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,000
There's one more thing.
There's a guy we didn't see yesterday.

147
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
I'm willing to bet he's the leader.

148
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
[Gon] What’s he look like?

149
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
[Killua] He's wearing a black coat
with an inverted cross on the back.

150
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
He has black, slicked-back hair.
I can't see his face.

151
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Damn it! They're really alert.

152
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
I'm too scared to circle around front.

153
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Give it to me. Where are you now?

154
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:32,000
[Killua] In front of the Motoba Building.
They're heading west on Continental.

155
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
[Kurapika] There's a station nearby.
Can you board their train?

156
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[Killua] Depends.
If it's crowded, I can manage.

157
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Hurry. Head to the south.

158
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
[munching] Okay!

159
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
[Killua] Melody's in the same car as them.

160
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
We're headed toward Castor.
I'm in the last car on the train.

161
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Heading to Castor?

162
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
The auction site's in that direction.

163
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
[Kurapika]
For that matter, so is our hotel.

164
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
[Squala]
Yeah. Yeah. I know, Eliza, I know.

165
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Honestly, I'm starting to get
pretty sick of this job!

166
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
I should be happy
I'm spending time with the dogs?

167
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Hmm. It sure beats taking care
of that spoiled brat, I guess.

168
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
I'm fond of Ms. Neon,
but she's just so... hyper.

169
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Look at this, Eliza!
It's so cute!

170
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
[grunts]

171
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[sighs] Well, won't be much longer.

172
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,000
-I'll find a better job, and--
-[growling]

173
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[knocking on door]

174
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
-[Squala] Who's there?
-[man] Room service.

175
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
[Squala] Leave it by the door.

176
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
[Squala whistles]

177
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
[dog growling and barking]

178
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Okay, let's eat.

179
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Man, I have really gotta find
another job and fast.

180
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
I don't have the energy
for this kind of work.

181
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:13,000
I just need to find something
that will support Eliza and these guys.

182
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
But that's easier said than done.

183
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
[dog whining]

184
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Huh?

185
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Don't worry, buddy.
I'll figure something out soon.

186
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
[phone vibrating]

187
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[Killua] They got off.

188
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
They got off at Liber Station,

189
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
and they're heading
for the Saloma Mall exit.

190
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Not good. The hotel is that way.

191
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[dialing]

192
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Seriously? They found out
we switched our rooms?

193
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,000
[groans] This isn't funny!
We need to get out of here now!

194
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
I better take these with me.

195
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
[Leorio] The station's over there.
Should we get a little closer?

196
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,000
[Kurapika] No.

197
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Any closer than this
then the Troupe might sense my hostility.

198
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Hey, Gon.
This is far as it’s safe to go.

199
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
I need to be this far from the station

200
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
or else they’ll notice me
before I want them to.

201
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
It'll take approximately 0.5 seconds
to land an attack.

202
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,000
And that’s more than enough time
for them to engage an evasive maneuver.

203
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Unless they're distracted, of course.

204
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
[both gasp]

205
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
The spiders!

206
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
It's moving. Descending slowly.

207
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
So, on an elevator. Are they leaving?

208
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Let's hurry up and get in there, then.

209
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
We will apprehend him as a group.

210
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Try to stay close enough
to provide assistance.

211
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Pakunoda, once we have him,
get the information on Uvo.

212
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Got it.

213
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
After that, Nobunaga, they're all yours.

214
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Go.

215
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
They're running there now.
And they're fast!

216
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Can we head them off by car?

217
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Well, it is evening rush hour.
At this rate,

218
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
-they might be a lot faster on foot.
-[car door opening]

219
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Huh? Kurapika!

220
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
I'll contact you soon. Wait till then!

221
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[Gon] Wait, Kurapika!
I have an idea! Kurapika, come on!

222
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Melody and I are still
at the station entrance.

223
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
But they just ran off to the northwest.

224
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Right. In pursuit.

225
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[Killua] Wait, you're chasing them?
That's dangerous!

226
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
They're gonna notice you! Knock it off!

227
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
You there! Damn! He hung up.
What the hell?

228
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
[women laughing]

229
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
[both gasp]

230
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[woman 1] Whoa, what's that?

231
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
[woman 2] Are those ninjas?

232
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
[Kortopi] Target is moving rapidly
toward two o'clock.

233
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Then he must be in a car.

234
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
I was going to wait
till I found another job.

235
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
But not now! Today's my last day!

236
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,000
[Killua] Leorio, where's Gon?

237
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
He took off after Kurapika.
He told us to wait here,

238
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
but there's no way in hell
I can just sit here doing nothing!

239
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
I'm driving to the Beitacle Hotel,
but I'm stuck in traffic!

240
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Grr! Fine, we'll go after 'em!
What is wrong with these people?

241
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Damn it! It's like they just do
whatever the hell they want!

242
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,000
We're being followed.

243
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Since when?

244
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Oops. I was too focused on the target.

245
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Is the chain user behind or in front?

246
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Nobunaga, Pakunoda and Kortopi,
go ahead.

247
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,000
[Pakunoda] Roger that.

248
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
[both gasp]

249
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
[Chrollo] See them?

250
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[Shizuku] Just shadows, not faces.
One of them's in the alley.

251
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
[Machi] The other's behind the trash can.

252
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
[Chrollo] Okay. Keep using Gyo.

253
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[both] Roger.

254
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
[Kurapika] Come on, spiders.
I'm ready.

255
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[Gon] Kurapika, stop!

256
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
We can't fight the three of them and win
if they know we're here! Don't do it!

257
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Guess I'll have to take my chances.

258
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[Kurapika] Gon?

259
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,000
I'm sorry, okay?
I'll stop following you. Just forget it!

260
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[Machi] Him again?

261
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:48,000
[Chrollo]
The one you mentioned. This is him?

262
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
The other one's here as well.
Come on out.

263
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
[thunder rumbling]

264
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Well? The Mafia reward has been canceled,
so what do you want with us?

265
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Really, it has? We didn't know!

266
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[thunder crashing]

267
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[Machi] What do we do, boss?

268
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
-[Chrollo] Seize them.
-[dialing]

269
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Phinks? It's me.

270
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Come to the Beitacle Hotel.

271
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
[Machi] Shouldn't we get rid of them here?

272
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
No, I have faith in your instincts.

273
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
If they're connected
to the chain user somehow,

274
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
we should keep them alive.

275
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
My instincts aren't all that trustworthy.

276
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
[Gon] Hey, can I ask you something?

277
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
How can you kill people
who have nothing to do with you?

278
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
[thunder crashing]

279
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,000
[Chrollo] You have a lot of hostility
for someone who's just surrendered.

280
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Perhaps because...
they've nothing to do with us? No.

281
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
On second thought, it's not that simple.

282
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:10,000
My motives are unimportant now.
I don’t like speaking of them.

283
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:16,000
But surprisingly enough,
or, as I expected...

284
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
The reason’s the key
to understanding myself.

285
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[Killua] What's he talking about?

286
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[Chrollo] Head to the hotel
and wait for Phinks and the others.

287
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
If they try to escape, kill them.

288
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,000
[Machi] Understood.

289
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,000
[Melody] Now that they're on high alert,
we have to keep our distance,

290
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,000
otherwise, they're bound to notice us.

291
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Make sure you're concealing your presence.

292
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
-Damn it!
-We just have to be patient.

293
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
-I'm aware of that!
-I don't think you are!

294
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Your reckless pursuit
exposed them to needless danger.

295
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Do you even know why they allowed
themselves be captured?

296
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,000
If you get caught here too, then no one
will be able to stop the Troupe!

297
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,000
[Kurapika breathing deeply]

298
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
I'm sorry.

299
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Humans all have to lower their guard
sooner or later.

300
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
You're no different. We must wait.

301
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
You're right.

302
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
[Melody] Where's Squala?

303
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[Kurapika sighs]
He's not answering his cell.

304
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
This is not the chain user.

305
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
No, but I recognize his face
from the list.

306
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Step outside!

307
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[Squala]
Well, I've got my fair share of skill.

308
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
I've survived some close calls.

309
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
That experience has given me
a sixth sense.

310
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Right now, it's telling me...

311
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,000
that today, I'm...

312
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[Nobunaga]
Make one move and I'll kill you.

313
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[Squala grunting]

314
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
I have questions I want you
to answer truthfully.

315
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,000
One of your associates uses chains,
doesn't he? Where is he?

316
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:10,000
What are you talking about?
And who are you, anyway?

317
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Do you realize
I'm with the Nostrade family-- [yells]

318
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Just answer the damn question,
or else your left's next.

319
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Hey! Didn't I tell you not to move?

320
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Stay still and answer
the woman's questions, you idiot.

321
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
What did you do to Uvogin?

322
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
The big guy that you
and your friends captured.

323
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:36,000
That guy? He escaped from us somehow.
After that, I have no idea!

324
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Where are the other bodyguards?

325
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,000
They already went back to the island.
I was on my way home too, when you guys--

326
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
-[Pakunoda grunts]
-[Squala yells]

327
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,000
-There's a penalty for lying.
-But I'm not lying!

328
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Why would I lie in a situation
like this one?

329
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,000
[Pakunoda] I'll ask you one more time.
Where is the chain user hiding?

330
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
[Squala] I don't know who you're talking
about. I don't know any chain user, okay?

331
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
One last question.

332
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Is there anyone you care for or love?

333
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Do you really think I'd be
in this business if there were?

334
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[Pakunoda] Hmm...

335
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Her name is Eliza.

336
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
[Squala gasps]

337
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
She's very... beautiful.

338
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[Squala sighs]

339
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
If any of you lay a finger--

340
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,000
[thunder rumbling]

341
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
I kept telling you not to move.

342
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Just wouldn't listen.

343
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:46,000
So, did you get any decent data
on the chain user?

344
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:51,000
It would be far too much trouble
to explain,

345
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,000
so I'll just shoot it into you...

346
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
with my Memory Bomb.

347
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
I'll stop if you're scared.

348
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Oh, shut up. Go ahead.

349
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,000
[Nobunaga] I see.

350
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
So that's what you look like,
Mr. Kurapika!

351
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:28,000
I'll remember your name and your face
until I get the chance to murder you!

352
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:36,000
[narrator] The Phantom Troupe has,
at last, identified Uvogin's killer.

353
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Kurapika races to rescue Gon and Killua.

354
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
The final battle draws near.

355
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[theme music playing]

356
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
-[Gon] Coming up, Gon...
-[Killua] And Killua's...

357
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

358
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-I'm Gon!
-I'm Killua!

359
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

360
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Today, we'll introduce Nobunaga.

361
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:06,000
He's an Enhancer and an Iaidō master
who uses a four-meter En radius.

362
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
His aura lets him take down foes
with one strike.

363
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
One strike?

364
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,000
[both] You're out!

365
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Initiative and Law."

366
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:21,000
[Killua] The keyword is dark adaptation.

367
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,000
-[Gon] What does it mean?
-[Killua] Look it up, dummy.
